  "notes": "Input sockets are XLR/6.35 mm combo jacks (mic, line or instrument via the LINE/INST switch where present). INSERT jacks are TRS send/return; the signal path through them is not modelled. Playback outputs are RCA. MIDI IN/OUT are 5-pin DIN. USB bus-powered. Routing: the MIX knob blends inputs with playback 1-2 on MAIN OUT; MONITOR A/B selects playback 1-2 or 3-4 for the headphones. Controls from the U-PHORIA Quick Start Guide, 'Step 2: Controls'. MIX sets the balance of the input signals against playback 1-2 at MAIN OUT and the headphones; MONITOR A/B puts playback 3-4 on the headphones; STEREO/MONO switches the input monitoring to mono. Modelling assumptions: MIX fully to INPUT means no playback on MAIN OUT, fully to PLAYBACK means no direct input signal; MAIN OUT and PHONES at MIN are silent; STEREO/MONO and MONITOR A/B are shown but do not change the paths here (which input goes to which side in stereo is not stated). The single +48 V switch is taken to feed all inputs.",
